@startuml 07-state-device
' pnt-edge: per-serial-device state (SerialInput::run_device, SAD section 6.4)
title Serial device lifecycle (one reader thread per device)
[*] --> opening
opening --> open : port.open() ok\nconfigure (UBX CFG-VALSET / VN-100 init)
opening --> closed : open fails
closed --> opening : after 1 s
open --> open : frame decoded\nstamp, enqueue to Merger
open --> no_data : nothing received for 5 s
no_data --> open : bytes arrive
open --> lost : read error\n(port closed, unplugged)
no_data --> lost : read error
lost --> opening : reopen loop
open --> [*] : stop()
no_data --> [*] : stop()
lost --> [*] : stop()
closed --> [*] : stop()

note right of open
  Health per device: state, detail,
  bytes, frames, decode errors,
  rate, age, last TOV -> StatusSnapshot
end note
@enduml
